  "sourceReproduction": "Six unchanged PNGs,28 selected generated source images, original shadow components, deterministic nearest sampling/current palette indexing/integer source composition,47 authored native slots and exact4/8-cell geometry. Child imports are source extraction only.",
  "visualReview": {
    "root": "Approved all three native-size sheets, including explicit separation, inversion and original shadow poses. Existing extended compressed storage plus explicit gfx89 stream accepted as integration direction.",
    "lead": "Approved all 47 native slots, enlarged Rootling 0–5 and Rider 18–23: coherent root crown/face, distinct snapping jaws across all three ramps, readable guard/mount separation and preserved shadows. Label spacing correction requested and completed.",
    "self": "Every native source pose and current palette inspected at 1× and enlarged scale; fixed label-only spacing; exact displayed cell/pixel tests, timed native execution and actual battle/demonstration captures inspected.",
    "scope": "Static source approval is separate from native timing, scene proof and production integration."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "The preserved palette words are the current approved recolors, not original CT colors. No new palette writes occur.",
    "All lowest opaque Y values are exact. Snap Briar slot 1 is one pixel shorter (29 rather than 30); other heights are exact. Width differences are explicit, with single-body center rounding up to 0.5 px and independently composed Rider total-center differences up to 2 px.",
    "Translated duplicate slots remain native duplicates: Rootling 13/15 and 14/16 differ by −12 Y; Rider corresponding pairs differ by −8 Y. Rider 15/16 are not referenced by AA158. Source mirrors are limited to audited original mirrors.",
    "Rider shadows in slots 18/19/21/23 reuse exact original indexed pixels under the current palette. Body and guard pixels are actual generated raster samples; no anatomy was drawn.",
    "Rider streaming delays 24 steady phase boundaries by exactly one video frame while displaying a coherent complete preceding frame. Original requests and timers are unchanged; visible timing is not claimed identical.",
